      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s early name Knipesville honored the Knipe family, who ran early farms and mills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/scotrun_pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The area receives about 47 inches of rain and 75 inches of snow annually, with lake‑effect snow often topping 100 inches in heavy winters.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/scotrun_pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Wildlife here includes the bog turtle, frosted elfin butterfly, and northern harrier, plus brook trout in streams and osprey over wetlands.",
